WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.767
Interpretability and alignment.

2
00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:09.833
The closest thing to a future proof frontier skill: deep, hiring now, and useful to systems you already build.

3
00:00:11.033 --> 00:00:17.000
Mechanistic interpretability reverse engineers what circuits inside a transformer really compute.

4
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:21.500
Think induction heads, attention head roles, and residual stream features.

5
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:26.833
It builds on attention mechanics, with real tools like TransformerLens and nnsight.

6
00:00:28.033 --> 00:00:30.433
Start with the most active research direction.

7
00:00:30.733 --> 00:00:32.364
Take a layer's activations.

8
00:00:32.364 --> 00:00:33.933
They are dense and opaque.

9
00:00:34.233 --> 00:00:39.033
A sparse autoencoder decomposes them into features a human can interpret.

10
00:00:39.333 --> 00:00:43.133
Then you can amplify or suppress one feature to steer behavior.

11
00:00:43.433 --> 00:00:46.333
This is already showing up in production safety tooling.

12
00:00:47.533 --> 00:00:50.267
Next, dangerous capability evaluations.

13
00:00:50.567 --> 00:00:54.343
They test what a model can do, not just what it usually does.

14
00:00:54.343 --> 00:00:56.633
Can it replicate itself autonomously?

15
00:00:56.933 --> 00:00:58.733
Can it carry out cyber attacks?

16
00:00:59.033 --> 00:01:00.825
Does it deceive under pressure?

17
00:01:00.825 --> 00:01:04.467
It is your eval discipline, applied to risk instead of quality.

18
00:01:05.667 --> 00:01:08.567
Scalable oversight asks: who checks the checker?

19
00:01:08.867 --> 00:01:11.167
One idea is debate between models.

20
00:01:11.167 --> 00:01:13.400
Here a user asks a hard question.

21
00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:15.167
Model A gives an answer.

22
00:01:15.467 --> 00:01:17.033
Model B points out the flaw.

23
00:01:17.333 --> 00:01:23.000
A human only has to verify the cited evidence, even when the models are better at the task.

24
00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:26.000
Why is it the best frontier bet?

25
00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:28.533
It compounds with everything else you learn.

26
00:01:28.833 --> 00:01:31.633
It needs no physics degree and no robot lab.

27
00:01:31.933 --> 00:01:35.600
And every serious AI organization is growing this function.

28
00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:37.588
Let's recap.

29
00:01:37.588 --> 00:01:41.267
Mechanistic interpretability reverse engineers circuits.

30
00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:44.267
Sparse autoencoders find features you can steer.

31
00:01:44.567 --> 00:01:46.933
Evals test dangerous capabilities.

32
00:01:47.233 --> 00:01:49.489
Oversight asks who checks the checker.

33
00:01:49.489 --> 00:01:51.567
Next up: where to spend your hours.
